From: prospero-win orbis <noreply@localhost>
Subject: server, ntdll: orbis: trace the first requests and the thread fd hand-over

Run 11 on the PS4 completed the client handshake (patch 1050's lines) and
then stalled in the first request: the server read init_first_thread and
the two fd messages, the client never got a reply. Which step failed is
not said by either side: a thread whose reply descriptor did not arrive is
killed without a word, and the client then reads its own reply pipe
forever (it still holds the write end). Orbis stderr lines, to remove with
patch 1050: the fd messages received (client fd, thread, server fd), the
inflight look-ups and O_NONBLOCK in init_thread, each of the first eight
requests with its status and whether a reply fd exists, the first replies
written, every thread killed with its last request, and on the client the
first eight requests sent with their status.

